2026-11-02  Greger Cronquist  <greger@zero-gravity.se>

	* Version 2.9

	* Added progressive JPEG decoding (SOF2), with restart intervals

	* Added :SCALE (1/2, 1/4, 1/8) to DECODE-IMAGE and DECODE-STREAM,
	using reduced inverse DCTs; progressive scans of unneeded frequencies
	are skipped

	* Added :ROW-CALLBACK to DECODE-IMAGE and DECODE-STREAM, to receive
	rows instead of an image array

	* The decoder decodes one row of MCUs at a time: memory use is the
	output image plus a few hundred kilobytes, progressive images included

	* Decoding is several times faster: buffered 64-bit bit reader with
	Huffman lookahead tables, IDCT writing into component planes with
	sparse and DC-only cases, fused upsampling and color conversion, file
	streams read in chunks

	* Optional NEON SIMD on SBCL/ARM64 (push :CL-JPEG-SIMD onto *FEATURES*)

	* Header values are validated before use; invalid data signals
	INVALID-JPEG-DATA, truncated data TRUNCATED-JPEG-DATA. Fixed buffer
	overflows on malformed files (YCCK marker on non-CMYK images, Huffman
	tables with too many codes, out-of-range progressive scan parameters,
	undefined Huffman tables)

	* Fixed sequential images with one scan per subsampled component,
	DC Huffman table selection, and images with more than four scans

	* Decoded samples are level shifted by 128 instead of 127

	* DESCRIPTOR-BYTE-READER, when set, supplies the input bytes

	* Added a test system: (asdf:test-system :cl-jpeg)

